1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,876
Think inflation is cooling off?

2
00:00:02,826 --> 00:00:09,538
That 3.4 percent official headline rate is a lie when you actually look at your everyday bills.

3
00:00:09,538 --> 00:00:18,451
The official story is that annual inflation slowed to 3.4 percent, while core inflation is down to 2.5 percent.

4
00:00:18,451 --> 00:00:22,105
But those CPI numbers strip out the real pain.

5
00:00:22,105 --> 00:00:29,402
The price of gasoline actually surged by 24.6 percent, driving massive fuel costs.

6
00:00:29,402 --> 00:00:32,391
And it gets worse at the grocery store.

7
00:00:32,391 --> 00:00:38,206
Cumulative grocery prices are 32 percent higher than they were in 2020.

8
00:00:38,206 --> 00:00:46,766
This forces average households to spend an extra 1200 to 1400 dollars more every single year.

9
00:00:46,766 --> 00:00:52,146
This means the classic fifty-thirty-twenty budgeting rule is completely broken.

10
00:00:52,146 --> 00:00:59,239
Instead of spending just half on needs, average household spending on basic necessities has skyrocketed.

11
00:00:59,239 --> 00:01:05,326
It now swallows 62 percent of average income, leaving almost nothing for savings.

12
00:01:05,326 --> 00:01:12,798
You must recalculate your actual needs bucket using these real fuel and grocery rates instead of generic advice.

13
00:01:12,798 --> 00:01:16,970
Stop relying on outdated formulas from 2020.

